Package: nvidia-smi-live-web
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: apiplant <releases@apiplant.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/apiplant/nvidia-smi-live
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: Live nvidia-smi monitor for the browser
 nvidia-smi-live-web runs a minimal local web server that streams live GPU
 snapshots — utilization, VRAM, temperature, power and fan, plus a
 per-process memory table — to a static Solid.js page that updates in place.
 It binds 127.0.0.1:7680 by default; pass --port to change it.
 .
 The binary links only libc and libgcc_s. It loads libnvidia-ml.so.1 from the
 NVIDIA driver at runtime via dlopen. It needs a working NVIDIA driver to do
 anything useful; there is no driver dependency to declare, because the
 driver packages differ per
 vendor and generation. It is built against glibc 2.35, so it needs Debian 12
 (bookworm) or newer, or Ubuntu 22.04 or newer.
 .
 The package ships a systemd unit, nvidia-smi-live-web.service, which
 `systemctl enable --now nvidia-smi-live-web` starts.
